    "tautomer_graphs": "ZHK/EHK retain carbonyl and hydrazone NH but invert exocyclic C=N relative orientation (carbonyl-side C and hydrazone terminal N are the stereo reference atoms). AE transfers that H to carbonyl O with ring aromatization and azo N=N. AK transfers that H to ring C4 with azo N=N. The supplied exact graphs conserve C22H15F3N4O for all7a forms. Include symmetry-equivalent C4 AK configurations as equal achiral-environment subcases, not different chemical formulas.",
    "H_mapping": "Use explicit_tautomer_atom_pairs_from_ZHK and mobile_H_and_NMR_maps. One tracked hydrogen900 moves N5→O1 or corresponding C4 in the mapped graphs. Other hydrogens remain attached to their corresponding heavy atoms; no change of total formula/charge is allowed.",
    "primary_spectral_matrix": "7a_ZHK,8a_ZHK,5g_ZHK in CHCl3 andDMF; 7a_ZHK/EHK/AE/AK in the same two media. Separate same-tautomer solvent shift and population-weighted shift.",
    "NMR_IR": "For all four7a forms calculate the homologous ring carbon13C (carbonyl C inHK/AK; C–OH inAE) and mobile-proton shielding/shift in CHCl3 andDMSO continua (experimental media CDCl3/DMSO-d6; isotope shifts not assumed modeled), with one common shielding reference. Calculate carbonyl andNH/OH mode assignments; solid IR is contextual and not quantitatively identical to isolated solution harmonic IR.",
    "experimental_resolution": "Use the experimental main-table absorption maxima below; NMR chemical-shift ranges and solid IR ranges are cross-observable functional-group constraints, not invented per-tautomer measured spectra.",
